The following is an overview over bugs within Bun's source map implementation. This bug is the root cause behind the following:

- bun run
  - Error locations are not pointing at the right character, or line.
    - Error locations can be off by hundreds of lines in the worst case.
  - Bun's VCSode extension (and the work JetBrains is putting to get debugging to work in their products) is unable to break on many lines.
- bun build
  - Browser debuggers are unable to break on many lines
  - Sourcemap analysis tools are unable to open some of Bun's generated source maps.

I've given some efforts to fix these, but I've realized none of this is a quick fix, and will need a much larger audit over every bit of sourcemap code.

## Incorrect Sourcemaps
Sourcemaps are generated incorrectly. A full pass over sourcemap generation in js_parser.zig or bundle_v2.zig should be done to figure out what is going wrong.

Figure A *(there are two spaces after the `-`)*
```ts
;(hello -  world);
```
Figure B
```ts
hello-
world
```

esbuild produces different sourcemaps despite identical JS output.
This is significant because remapping sources does not map the same, some maps are off, some do not map at all.

`demo.sh`
```ts
