bunx esbuild '/Users/dave/hello/min.js' --platform=browser --outdir=esbuild --sourcemap=external
bun dump_maps.js
diff --color bun.map esbuild.map
```
`dump_maps.js`
```ts
import { SourceMapConsumer} from 'source-map';
import { readFileSync, writeFileSync } from 'fs';

async function dump(from, to, off = 0) {
    const data = JSON.parse(readFileSync(from, 'utf8'));
    await SourceMapConsumer.with(data, null, async(map) => {
        let out = '';
        map.eachMapping((m) => {
            out += `${m.source} ${m.originalLine}:${m.originalColumn} -> ${m.generatedLine + off}:${m.generatedColumn}\n`;
        });
        await writeFileSync(to, out);
    });
}

await dump('bun/min.js.map', 'bun.map', -1);
await dump('esbuild/min.js.map', 'esbuild.map', );
```

This is more than just adding brace close locations (the initial assumption), but a more fundamental issue in the sourcemaps.

## JSC vs V8 Stack Differences
This seems to only be visible when accessing error.stack. No idea why; More investigation is needed.

While not a issue in source maps, having 1:1 stack traces with `error.stack` is a goal of Bun, especially since we modified `error.stack` to print a v8 style stack trace.

In JSC/Safari, the column number of function calls are at the index before the `(`, where in v8/Node/Deno, this is located at the start of the identifier.

```ts
  hello()
//^    ^
//v8   jsc
```

This difference is visible in Bun's `error.stack` but only there, doing `console.log` (our formatter instead of error.stack) on the error works fine. I'm confused why this is only an issue in one part, considering JSC in no place reports the v8 style error column numbers.

## 1.0.15 Regression

Potentially caused by source mapping bugs, this is a regression in 1.0.15, when I was first made aware of how broken the sourcemaps are. I am not marking this issue as a whole as a regression, as I haven't found a single build of bun where the sourcemap generation was correct.

