### What steps can reproduce the bug?

The implementation of OutgoingMessage.setHeader in Node has a [special case handling](https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/309924f65d3cfa562a49fca8667f58fdea2759a6/lib/_http_outgoing.js#L733) of setting a Set-Cookie value when passing an array of header values, which seems to be missing from Bun's implementation. This leads to the resulting Set-Cookie headers being written as comma-separated values instead of separate headers.

MRE code below.

```js
import http from 'node:http';

const server = http.createServer();
server.on('request', (_, res) => {
    http.OutgoingMessage.prototype.setHeader.call(res, 'Set-Cookie', ['foo=bar', 'hello=world']);
    res.end();
});

server.on('listening', async () => {
    const res = await fetch('http://localhost:3000');
    res.headers.forEach((value, name) => {
        console.log(`${name}: ${value}`);
    });
    process.exit();
});

server.listen(3000);
```

