### What is the issue?

Currently, we already have guide to develop apps using Nuxt: [Build an app with Nuxt and Bun](https://bun.sh/guides/ecosystem/nuxt). This already works okay for development (use `--bun` flag to run `nuxt dev` using Bun instead of Node.js).

However, if the app uses packages that exports Bun-specific exports (e.g. Elysia), the app will break in production:

```
$ bun --bun .output/server/index.mjs
error: Cannot find package 'elysia' from '/home/tkesgar/git/tkesgar/nuxt-elysia/playground/.output/server/index.mjs'

Bun v1.2.5 (Linux x64)
```

This is because the default `node-server` preset in Nitro (Nuxt's underlying server framework) does not bundle the `bun` exports:

```json
{
  "exports": {
    ".": {
      "types": "./dist/index.d.ts",
      "bun": "./dist/bun/index.js",
      "import": "./dist/index.mjs",
      "require": "./dist/cjs/index.js"
    }
  }
}
```

![Bun exports does not get bundled by Nitro](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d480a97d-1acb-47a1-a08d-9f689fb065ed)

The solution is to add [Nitro Bun preset](https://nitro.build/deploy/runtimes/bun) in `nuxt.config.ts`:

```ts
// nuxt.config.ts
export default defineNuxtConfig({
  nitro: {
    preset: 'bun'
  }
})
```

